                        "entry_id": "f19468fd-bdeb-3d13-8980-d74e8e12c64d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abbreviation or diminutive for baronet, later replaced by Bt. It is a post-nominative title; the pre-nominative is Sir (e.g. Sir John Smith Bart.)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdc444f6-2813-4587-858e-8b277cbe640f",
                                "sense_id": "425954aa-8f10-3376-b639-57fc0fc1892a",
                                "text": "The First Lord's daughter proud,\nSnubbed earls and viscounts nightly—\nShe sneered at barts aloud.\nAnd spurned poor Joe Golightly."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
